.TH snip-gist 1 "" "snip 0.6.2" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-gist \- publish snippets through GitHub Gists
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip gist\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip gist push\fR [\fB\-\-public\fR] [\fB\-\-desc\fR] [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-readme\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-web\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip gist url\fR [\fB\-\-copy\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip gist status\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISELECTOR\fR] 
\fBsnip gist attach\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> <\fIGIST\fR> 
\fBsnip gist detach\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip gist delete\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip gist open\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Publish snippets through the GitHub gh CLI. push creates or updates a gist, url prints its link, status compares local content with the last push, attach adopts an existing gist, detach forgets the local record, delete removes the remote gist, and open launches a browser.
.PP
Gists are secret unless \-\-public is used at creation. GitHub cannot change an existing gist's visibility. \-\-new creates a different gist and leaves the old one online; gist delete is irreversible. These operations require gh to be installed and authenticated.
.PP
After a successful push, snip records the filenames it owns, the note and README inclusion choices, pushed_at, and a pushed_digest of the canonical publication payload. Local status rebuilds that digest to report clean or modified without contacting GitHub. A matching push is skipped as unchanged unless \-\-force is supplied; an attached gist has no pushed digest until it is pushed by snip.
.PP
The digest sorts published filenames in ascending UTF\-8 byte order and covers their length\-prefixed names and contents followed by the description. Its 32\-byte BLAKE3 value is stored as exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. See sniplib(5) for the complete contract.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip gist"
Publish snippets to GitHub Gists through the gh CLI
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip gist push"
Create the snippet's gist, or update it when one already exists
.TP
\fB\-\-public\fR
List the gist publicly. Only applies when creating; gist visibility cannot be changed afterwards
.TP
\fB\-\-desc\fR \fI<DESC>\fR
Gist description. Defaults to the snippet title, then to the description recorded by the previous push
.TP
\fB\-\-new\fR
Publish a new gist and replace the recorded one, leaving the old gist on GitHub
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-notes\fR
Publish fragment notes as separate Markdown files
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-readme\fR
Leave the snippet README out of the gist
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-web\fR
Open the gist in a browser afterwards
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR \fI<IF_HASH>\fR
Refuse the push unless the snippet still has this fingerprint
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Push even when the gist already matches the snippet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip gist url"
Print the URL of the snippet's gist
.TP
\fB\-\-copy\fR
Copy the URL to the clipboard as well as printing it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip gist status"
Report whether a snippet's gist is current
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Report every snippet in the library that has a gist
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR
Also fetch the gist from GitHub and report whether it still exists
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fISELECTOR\fR]
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip gist attach"
Record an existing gist as this snippet's gist
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.TP
<\fIGIST\fR>
Gist ID or URL
.SS "snip gist detach"
Forget a snippet's gist without deleting it on GitHub
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip gist delete"
Delete the snippet's gist on GitHub and forget it
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Delete without prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip gist open"
Open the snippet's gist in a browser
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Create or update a secret gist and print its URL:
.RS 4
.nf
snip gist push Brewfile
snip gist url Brewfile
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check every linked snippet without network access, then check one remotely:
.RS 4
.nf
snip \-\-output json gist status \-\-all
snip gist status Brewfile \-\-remote
.fi
.RE
